<title>USA: CBOT rice closes up on short-covering, cash firm.</title>
<headline>CBOT rice closes up on short-covering, cash firm.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>CBOT rice futures closed higher on short-covering and on a firm cash market relative to futures, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market shook off commercial selling and was converging to cash,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Rice futures volume was estimated at 450 contracts, down from 738 Thursday, according to the CBOT.</p>
<p>Rice closed six to 11 cents per cwt higher, with November up 11 at $10.12 per cwt.</p>
<p>Sam Nelson 312-408-8721</p>
